On Bedrock, a Claude id that yoagent has a preset for now sends its model's output maximum as inferenceConfig.maxTokens when you haven't set a cap. With --thinking on, that cap is now larger than the thinking budget.

• Implementation: a new helper, providers::bedrock_max_tokens, reads the cap from yoagent's own Bedrock preset rather than keeping a separate table. The Bedrock branch in src/agent_builder.rs changed by three lines to call it. I read configure_agent and it applies a user cap without clamping it, so setting the value again afterwards changes nothing when you gave a cap.
• Tests: three new tests run the real binary against the local recording stub, so no request goes to AWS:
  • With thinking on, the preset cap goes out and is larger than the budget.
  • With thinking off, the preset cap still goes out.
  • A cap you set (20000) is sent unchanged.

  The older test still shows amazon.nova-pro-v1:0 sending no cap. A unit test checks that the ids which get a cap and the ids yoyo warns about as guesses never overlap, so the warning stays true.
• Choice made: the cap is sent always for these ids, not only with thinking on, and the code comment explains why.
